Title: lua-https over Mbed TLS
Repository: love
Base: def245102c67909f9902095af613b1ae05249b62
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-21
Author: aros-loeve project
Problem: lua-https (require "https") was left out on AROS: its backends are the system HTTP clients of other platforms, curl or OpenSSL loaded at run time, and its plain connection uses C library socket calls AROS does not have. Games that fetch data over HTTPS could not.
Change: New backend MbedTLSConnection for AROS on Mbed TLS from the aros-crypto kit (CMake option AROS_CRYPTO_KIT, linked statically). src/libraries/aros/aros_net.c opens TCP connections through the calling thread's bsdsocket.library base and runs TLS over them: the server chain is checked against the system CA bundle ENV:SYS/Certificates/ca-bundle.crt and has to name the host; without the bundle, without a working random number source or with a certificate that fails the check the request fails (status 0) and the reason goes to stderr. Mbed TLS gets its locks before main(). PlaintextConnection uses the same TCP calls on AROS. LOVE_ENABLE_LUAHTTPS is on for AROS.
Scope: AROS (all targets)
Upstream: local-only
Verification: mainline x86_64 (nightly 2026-11-15, exec 51.17, pool slot v1-3), 2026-11-21, check game docs/evidence/2026-11-21-https/hgame: https://example.com/ 200 from the main thread and from a love.thread, https://www.wikipedia.org/ answers (403, it wants a User-Agent), expired, wrong-host and self-signed certificates of badssl.com refused with the reason printed, http://example.com/ 200; the game exits cleanly. Not run: Raspberry Pi, a system without a network stack or without the CA bundle, POST with a body, large downloads.
Removal: not planned
